test
## Setup

    ./setup.sh

This creates a `.venv/` virtualenv and installs the dependencies from
`requirements.txt` (librosa, matplotlib, numpy, soundfile, pillow, ipykernel).

Manually, if you prefer:

    python3 -m venv .venv
    .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt

Then select `.venv` as the kernel when opening `prepare_datasets.ipynb`.
